# Hermes Grok Tools Setup

When the user gives this repository URL and asks Cursor to set it up, clone the repo and run:

macOS / Linux:

```bash
./install.sh
```

Windows native PowerShell:

```powershell
.\install.ps1
```

The installer detects Cursor where possible and installs the repository plugin as a local Cursor plugin under `~/.cursor/plugins/local/hermes-grok-tools`. It does not use direct `cursor --add-mcp` registration.

For team distribution, use Cursor Dashboard > Settings > Plugins > Team Marketplaces and import the GitHub repository URL. The repository contains `.cursor-plugin/marketplace.json` and `plugins/hermes-grok-tools/.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`.

If auto-detection fails, run:

```bash
./install.sh --target cursor
```

Windows native:

```powershell
.\install.ps1 -Target cursor
```
